# Workspace Recipe LLM Guide

## Purpose

Inspect, validate, preview, and render local recipes.

## When To Run

- During first-run setup before creating files.
- Before hand-writing shape.
- When validating recipe changes.

## How To Read The Result

- Listing shows available recipes.
- Summary shows inputs and targets.
- Check validates metadata and rendering.
- Dry run shows create/skip status without writing.
- Shell preview shows rendered shell content.
- Recipes may compose `fragment` recipes through `includes`.

## Examples

- First-run path: `enclosure workspace recipe --list`, `enclosure workspace recipe <name> --show`, then `enclosure workspace recipe <name> <path> --shell`.
- Inspect recipes before creating files manually.
- Keep module-to-role ownership in `workspace.recipe.roles_map`.
- Provide required inputs as variables.
- If dry run skips a target, preserve, rename, or edit manually.
- If check fails, fix the recipe before attempting generation.

## Agent Tips

- Prefer a local recipe over inventing scaffolding.
- Inspect a recipe before rendering it.
- Use `--shell` when the recipe is the convention oracle.
- Run check or dry run before writing generated files.
